      "title": "UV dose damages microbial DNA",
      "description": "UV-C light near 254 nm damages the DNA/RNA of bacteria, viruses and protozoa (Cryptosporidium, Giardia) so they cannot reproduce. Dose = intensity × exposure time (mJ/cm²; drinking water often ≈ 40 mJ/cm²). UV leaves no residual, so a small chlorine dose is often added for the distribution network; water UV transmittance and sleeve fouling control performance.",
